Dear Roger,

Julie and I have checked the 32 transcriptions against the copies and correct=
ed the English at seven passages. Two of those corrections change the account=
 of conditions in Chapter 2, so I have replaced the two provisional paragraph=
s and attached the revised note, together with the seven passages in French a=
nd English.

Could you look particularly at CR/13/A f. 085r, ll. 3=E2=80=935? The invitati=
on allows one companion per member; the heating gift is voluntary and the nex=
t sentence welcomes those who give nothing. I had treated it as a charge for =
the guest's admission.

At CR/14/A f. 186r, ll. 7=E2=80=939, read with the preceding sentences, the a=
rrears are to be collected before a book leaves the room. The member may stil=
l read on the premises. My earlier paragraph had put payment before entry. Th=
e revised note keeps those two conditions distinct and leaves the question of=
 actual visits open until we have independent evidence.

Best,
Judith

